# Line endings.
#
# The blobs in this repo are LF, as they should be. The problem this file
# solves is local-only: with core.autocrlf=true (the Git-for-Windows
# default) a Windows checkout smudges those LF blobs to CRLF in the
# WORKING TREE, and `gofmt -l .` then flags every Go file. Linux CI is
# unaffected, so the result is a formatting gate that is green in CI and
# unusably noisy on a Windows dev box.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF on every platform, so local gofmt
# agrees with CI and the autocrlf setting stops mattering.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the file types that care.
*.go       text eol=lf
*.mod      text eol=lf
*.sum      text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
LICENSE    text eol=lf
NOTICE     text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts must keep CRLF or cmd.exe mis-parses them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mov  binary
*.webm binary
*.ico  binary

# Golden files pin normalized output byte for byte; an eol rewrite would
# silently invalidate them, so keep them LF like everything else and let
# `go test -update` be the only thing that changes them.
internal/moderate/adapters/**/testdata/*.golden text eol=lf

# Keep generated/vendored noise out of language stats and diffs.
docs/history/**    linguist-documentation
docs/superpowers/** linguist-documentation
